ts_url":"https://api.github.com/users/physicsvigilante/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Draft M37a — new JEE-relevant grounded-wire-current observable\n\n**Frozen charter BEFORE code:** `docs/m37a_charter.md` committed at `89dae06df53403a8fab6743ad8bdcc10fc76c514`.\n**Released base:** M36e merge `dc347251c14e449c53d51820b4481d1bfbee2cfb`, Git tree `60b4f21aa88a2031ec50c5d1e7c15a5135a7becf`, 20/20 real main-push CI passed.\n\nM37a adds **a new ideal quasistatic ground-wire current observer**, not a new 3D electrostatic solver or fake motion animation. Existing exact Kelvin ground-sphere and M13 force/energy are observed at each source position. A teacher-supplied instantaneous velocity gives only `I_sphere→ground=-q a v_radial/d²` (conventional positive-charge direction); true radial `I(t)` consumes actual M16a trajectories, verifies the full timeline against fresh M16a integration, and retains real elapsed time, energy, guard and source model. Signed induced charge `Q_sphere=-q a/d` is derived from the native physical solution. No wire resistance, EM delay, radiation or surface-contact dynamics.\n\n**Novel evidence:** independent SI force `F_r=-k q² a d/(d²-a²)²`, mechanical energy `U=-k q² a/[2(d²-a²)]`, native-position charge derivative `-dQ/dt`; positive/negative incoming/outgoing/tangential, translated and rotated geometry, permittivity, actual RK4 radial time series, near-surface guard, hostile false sign/charge/velocity/energy/time/provenance refusals. Independent stdlib JSON physics checker imports **no conductor_sim**. Dedicated Python 3.10/3.12 workflow plus full inherited CI required.\n\n**JEE fidelity:** the M36a audit lists physical p8 Multiple Correct Q21 in `02_conductors_half_size.pdf` as partial. No unreviewed claim of the problem's complete source wording/answer or numeric givens; this PR is a reusable *current observable* first. Original source page and answer need independent visual inspection in review.\n\n**DO NOT MERGE OR MARK READY** until current exact-head source CI (full Python 3.10/3.12, historical browser, real FEMM 5, new M37a physics), completed risk-scoped independent scientific evidence checks, explicit owner authorization, exact-head merge and postmerge main-push CI. Unrelated physics/solver/renderer files remain unchanged.\n\nSee [M37a charter](docs/m37a_charter.md), [design + limits](docs/m37a.md), `src/conductor_sim/grounded_sphere_wire.py`, `tests/test_m37a_grounded_wire_current.py`, `tools/m37a_ground_wire_reference.py`, and `examples/grounded_sphere_wire_current.py`.\n\n\n### Independent review history — one R4 continuation, no fresh broad audit\n\n**CURRENT exact source HEAD:** `73d7daee9f31f6feee3e6305205aa28abc3e48af`. **Actual native Git TREE:** `c728041ca5118013c6979d120c8805f31ee09fa0`. PR remains draft and unmerged.\n\nThe original independent [R1](https://github.com/physicsvigilante/review_sandbox/pull/6), [R2](https://github.com/physicsvigilante/review_sandbox/pull/7), [R3](https://github.com/physicsvigilante/review_sandbox/pull/8) and two [R4 reviewer executions](https://github.com/physicsvigilante/review_sandbox/actions/runs/44326169759) retain their own original FAILED evidence and old exact-source identities. Reviews of the underlying Kelvin image force/current/energy, M16a integration, and source workbook p8 Q21 (prescribed constant-speed approach, key (1),(3)) remain valid for those **unchanged physical source files**; no new whole-problem score is claimed.\n\nThe latest independent R4 executable reviewer challenge rejected the original false t=0 turning-point event and all prior signed charge, unit, identity, guard, drift and event forgeries, and accepted genuine elapsed-time histories. It found **one newly accepted forged event:** same exact stored timestamp and zero reported velocity, but a different event displacement/physical position from the stored particle. R4 workflow failure is retained; there is NOT a PASS report.\n\n**CURRENT narrow correction:** at a coincident stored timestamp a turning event must have the **same SI displacement AND physical position as the stored particle**, in addition to its existing zero-velocity and outward→inward signed velocity bracketing. The author added a direct regression reproducing the reviewer’s previously accepted zero-velocity/mismatched-position falsification and another position/displacement variant. Only `tools/m37a_ground_wire_reference.py`, `tests/test_m37a_grounded_wire_current.py`, and `docs/m37a.md` changed since R4, NOT the public physics solver, M16a integrator, FEMM5, renderer or original PDF.\n- Current source-pinned **developer-controlled** M37a Python 3.10/3.12 **123/123 focused tests PASS**, genuine CLI JSON and stdlib independent Kelvin SI checker PASS. Full same-HEAD 25 production PR/push workflows must finish terminal SUCCESS; incomplete checks do not confer release.\n- **Continue the SAME independent review #04** using the reviewer’s prior self-authored harness, preserving failed R4 attempts and no redundant full physics audit: [EXACT-HEAD R4 CONTINUATION PROMPT](https://github.com/physicsvigilante/review_sandbox/blob/main/projects/conductor_sim/pr-89/REVIEWER-PROMPT-04B.md). Request a final independent `review-04-chat-b.md` with new exact Git TREE and current CI; older red runs remain negative evidence.\n\n**No merge, no READY state and no owner approval.** A genuine targeted R4 PASS plus full current-head CI can support a separate explicit owner merge decision, expected-head protection, identical reviewed source tree on main, and complete postmerge main-push CI.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-18T12:21:06Z","updated_at":"2026-11-18T14:56:09Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"41484c57d3f7f3b9e7a34ee134e9e9215c42c28c","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"physicsvigilante:m37a-grounded-sphere-